: "3", "text": "Asset, shared record, user interface and service perform different roles."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Token is the asset, DemoNet-A supplies the shared record, WindowWallet is the interface, RiverDesk is the service. Correct every role; an interface is not itself the asset's ledger."}, {"id": "KC01A-2", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Authorisation precedes the supplied network processing and separate provider checks."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Provider credit establishes authorisation before the network records its request."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Opening WindowWallet establishes completed provider credit before any network processing."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Opening WindowWallet establishes that its provider has accepted the request and already completed receiving-account credit."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Permission, network processing and service accounting are distinct stages."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "An internal credit must occur before any authorisation."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Permission precedes the described network processing/record; service credit follows its own checks. Opening an interface does not establish later stages."}, {"id": "KC01A-3", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "RiverDesk's update creates another token network."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "RiverDesk's update replaces every network record."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "RiverDesk updates its internal account after its checks."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A service can update its own accounting without that update being a new on-chain transfer."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2",