ole must be read rather than inferred from “crypto.”"}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Fee assets have no relationship to the selected network."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: DEMO-UNIT is the supplied token; it does not replace Ethereum's stated native fee asset by merely being crypto."}, {"id": "KC01B-6", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Choose the unavailable familiar route because its quote is lower."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Choose the available token route conditionally, accepting the supplied cost/privacy/recovery limits."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Decline the token route because no valid situation can use it."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Higher cost guarantees recovery."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Addresses omit account names, so the public event guarantees private identity."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Access changes this comparison; cost, visibility and recovery still constrain it."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: The recipient cannot use the cheaper familiar route. The available token route fits this access requirement conditionally, with its cost, public-event and recovery limits."}, {"id": "KC01B-7", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Promise a reversal if the interface remains installed."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Promise a reversal because the recipient has an account."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Make no guaranteed-recovery claim for this route."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "No reversal guarantee is supplied, despite access being available."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Access alone creates a refund obligation."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The recipient uses an installed provider interface, so that interface can cancel the original ledger event whenever recovery is requested."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Availability is not guaranteed reversal. Continue a comparison without inventing a recovery promise."}], "outcomes": ["O-01.1", "O-01.2", "O-01.3", "O-01.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-02-A", "canonical_id": "KC-02", "kind": "check", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-02", "title": "Inspect the claim, then the authority", "fixture_html": "<p>Fixture: A message carrying a copied <strong>HarbourHelp</strong> logo says, “Only ten minutes left. Pay a 4 <code>DEMO-CASH</code> release charge and receive a guaranteed 30% return tomorrow.” It links to <code>DEMO-SENDER-LINK</code> and asks for a recovery phrase. A second request says “No phrase needed; no visible fee,” but its mock authority panel grants an unrelated party unlimited spending of <code>DEMO-TOKEN</code>. Your independently stored HarbourHelp bookmark reaches the genuine mock account support panel. A sender screenshot says 20 tokens paid; your independently opened receiving record says <strong>Pending</strong>, no credit. Later a second receiving record independently shows <strong>Credited, 20 DEMO-TOKEN, matching DEMO-REF-21</strong>; no local payout record is supplied.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC02A-1", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The guaranteed return and deadline warrant independent verification."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The countdown verifies that the branded opportunity has a limited allocation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The precise stated percentage verifies the return for this particular offer."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The precise percentage and countdown independently substantiate the promised return."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Time pressure and an unsubstantiated guaranteed return are relevant warning indicators."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every message with a date is fraudulent."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Ten-minute pressure and an unsubstantiated guaranteed return are relevant indicators. Do not claim all dated messages are scams."}, {"id": "KC02A-2", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pay the release fee after checking the familiar logo against your account."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use the matching logo to verify identity before paying the release charge."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Flag copied identity and the advance charge as warning indicators."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A logo can be imitated; an advance charge does not establish entitlement."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A small initial payment proves a large return is guaranteed."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The matching logo connects the release charge to the familiar account, making the advance payment adequate proof of entitlement."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: The copied logo is not independent identity evidence, and paying first does not establish a guaranteed entitlement."}, {"id": "KC02A-3", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Open the sender's link to ask whether it is genuine."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use the independently stored bookmark and genuine mock support panel."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use a sponsored result displaying the same logo."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "An advert guarantees the sender's authority."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The sender's link displays the familiar logo and can answer support questions, so its confirmation is independent identity verification."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Independently reached known support avoids relying on the message's channel."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Use the independently stored trusted route to genuine mock support, rather than sender links or sponsored branding."}, {"id": "KC02A-4", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Refuse the sender's request for recovery material."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Share selected recovery words to verify support without making an immediate transfer."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Share recovery material after confirming the request displays no network fee."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Entering recovery material without a network fee cannot affect spending control."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Recovery material can confer control and must not be handed to an external requester."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A partial disclosure is always safe in every recovery model."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Refuse external recovery-material disclosure. Neither a support claim nor fee absence changes its control significance."}, {"id": "KC02A-5", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Grant the request because no phrase is shown."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Grant it because no visible fee is shown."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Decline the unexplained unlimited authority."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Permissions can have consequences without exposing a secret or charging a visible fee."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A phrase is the only way spending control can be affected."}, {"id