": "2", "text": "Any prior Pending state prevents later credit forever."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Matching provider credit also establishes the separate local-currency payout."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Matching independent Credited evidence establishes this provider credit. It does not establish local payout or another transaction."}], "outcomes": ["O-02.1", "O-02.2", "O-02.3", "O-02.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-02-B", "canonical_id": "KC-02", "kind": "check", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-02", "title": "Verification can establish a legitimate notice", "fixture_html": "<p>Fixture: A purported <strong>BridgeAccount</strong> representative says, “Today only: guaranteed double return. Pay an activation deposit through <code>DEMO-AD-LINK</code>.” The branding matches your account, but identity is unverified. You independently navigate using an existing trusted bookmark to your mock account. Its support panel confirms a <strong>separate ordinary maintenance notice</strong>, requiring no money, secrets or permission; the double-return offer is absent. One external requester asks for a private key. Another “zero-fee login” request authorises a named outsider to spend all <code>DEMO-UNIT</code>; its purpose is unexplained. A sender's 11-token screenshot has no receiving record. A different claim has independently checked credit of 8 <code>DEMO-UNIT</code> matching <code>DEMO-REF-33</code>.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC02B-1", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "A doubled return is guaranteed because a deadline is stated."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Short-deadline and guaranteed-return language warrant verification."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Maintenance notices prove all investment claims are legitimate."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Urgency and unsupported certainty are warning indicators, not proof of a return."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The short deadline indicates a limited verified allocation, so the sender's precise time establishes the double-return offer is genuine."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The absence of a phrase request guarantees honesty."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Unsupported doubling and short-deadline language warrant verification. A legitimate maintenance notice does not substantiate yield."}, {"id": "KC02B-2", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Flag impersonation potential and the advance activation deposit."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat matching branding as verified identity."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Pay first to determine whether the sender is genuine."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Sending the activation charge lets the branded account prove it receives funds, which independently establishes the representative's identity."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Any logo match proves account ownership."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Copied branding and an advance-payment request do not establish legitimacy."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Branding can be copied; the requested activation deposit is an advance charge, not identity proof."}, {"id": "KC02B-3", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept both notices after confirming maintenance in the genuine support panel."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept the advertised offer because its branding matches the confirmed maintenance notice."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Confirm maintenance only; keep the unrelated offer unverified."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Independent verification never confirms a legitimate notice."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The independent panel confirms one notice, not the unrelated offer."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Independent maintenance confirmation also verifies the offer using that same brand."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Independent support confirms only the actual maintenance notice. Recognise a verified legitimate claim without transferring its status to an unrelated offer."}, {"id": "KC02B-4", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Send the private key if the requester calls it a support code."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Refuse the external private-key request."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Send it because no funds are requested immediately."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A support label cannot make spending-control material safe to disclose."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Support uses the term code instead of key, so that field serves only an account-reference purpose rather than spending control."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "An absence of immediate payment means no control can be affected."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Private-key disclosure is refused even when renamed a support code. No actual key is collected or entered."}, {"id": "KC02B-5", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Decline the unexplained outsider spending permission."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept because the visible fee is zero."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept because the request is labelled login."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Login labels prove a request has no authority."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "This login panel displays no network fee or immediate transfer, so accepting the outsider's permission cannot affect later spending."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Read the actual authority; signature/permission consequences differ from secret disclosure."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Read the stated outsider authority and decline it. A login label/zero visible fee is not proof of harmlessness."}, {"id": "KC02B-6", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Release goods for the 11-token screenshot immediately."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Infer that 11 tokens are permanently lost."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Obtain the independent receiving evidence for that specific claim."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The sender image supplies the same evidence as the recipient account."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The sender's image alone does not establish receipt or permanent loss."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A missing record guarantees future credit."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Obtain independent evidence for the 11-token claim. The image alone supports neither credit nor permanent loss."}, {"id": "KC02B-7", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Keep the eight-token payment unverified because the eleven-token claim has no record."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Recognise only the specific matching eight-token account credit."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use the eight-token credit to confirm the eleven-token screenshot from the same sender."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Credit evidence must match the amount/reference of the actual claim."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The same sender already produced an eight-token credit, so that credit independently verifies the later eleven-token screenshot as well."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Independent receiving evidence can never establish account credit."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: The matching 8-token record supports that specific credit, not the separate 11-token claim. Reconcile claim, reference and amount."}], "outcomes": ["O-02.1", "O-02.2", "O-02.3", "O-02.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-03-A", "canonical_id": "KC-03", "kind": "check", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-03", "title": "Control determines the recovery route", "fixture_html": "<p>Fixture: <strong>DeskAccount</strong> is custodial: the provider controls spending authorisation, supplies account access and offers identity-based account recovery subject to its policy. <strong>PhrasePocket</strong> is self-custody: the user controls authorisation; a local password unlocks this device, while its recovery phrase restores the described account on another compatible device. The provider cannot reset that phrase-based control. <strong>GuardianCircle</strong> is a separate alternative model: recovery requires two of three previously configured guardians; no recovery phrase is used in this fixture. Two guardians are currently reachable. No model guarantees recovery in all circumstances.</p>\n<p>Labelled placeholders: <code>DEMO-ADDRESS</code> = public receiving identifier; <code>DEMO-KEY</code> = private spending key; <code>DEMO-PHRASE</code> = PhrasePocket recovery material; <code>DEMO-LOCAL-PASS</code> = PhrasePocket device password; <code>DEMO-ACCOUNT-PASS</code> = DeskAccount login password. All values are inert labels, never actual credentials. Address sharing can affect privacy even though it is not secret spending material.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC03A-1", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "DeskAccount's user directly controls its network key; the provider has no role."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "PhrasePocket's interface company controls every user's key."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The provider controls DeskAccount authorisation; the user controls PhrasePocket authorisation."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Control follows the supplied custody model, not whether both have an app."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "DeskAccount and PhrasePocket both present password-protected phone interfaces, so the same party must control their underlying network authorisation."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A device screen always proves direct control of the network key."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Provider controls DeskAccount network authorisation; user controls PhrasePocket. The shared presence of an app does not decide custody."}, {"id": "KC03A-2", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "DeskAccount depends on its provider; PhrasePocket assigns secret-control duties to its user."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "DeskAccount and PhrasePocket both depend on the provider resetting network control after loss."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "PhrasePocket needs no backup duties because the ledger retains its balance after device loss."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The shared wallet-app category gives providers recovery control for both accounts."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Custody changes provider dependence and the user's responsibilities."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A local password is a universal recovery guarantee."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: DeskAccount depends on provider policy/operation, while PhrasePocket puts the supplied secret-control responsibilities on its user. Neither model has an unconditional reset."}, {"id": "KC03A-3", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Address, key and phrase are all ordinary public receipt data."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Address is a receiving identifier; key/phrase are secret control material."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Key is the public destination; address is the recovery phrase."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Every labelled field can authorise spending equally."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The receiving address does not display a name, so sharing its related activity cannot reveal any connection to the user."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Receiving information and secret control/recovery material have different purposes."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Address is a receiving identifier, key/phrase are control/recovery secrets. The address can still have privacy consequences."}, {"id": "KC03A-4", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Share both passwords with support because neither field is labelled a private key."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use the DeskAccount login password to restore PhrasePocket control on a replacement device."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Protect both passwords; local unlocking and provider login are different functions."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Local unlocking and provider login are different access functions; neither should be disclosed."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Both passwords protect wallet access, so either restores spending on another device."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A password becomes public whenever support requests it."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Local password unlocks the supplied device; provider password logs in to the supplied service. Protect both and do not substitute either for unrelated recovery material."}, {"id": "KC03A-5", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use PhrasePocket's protected phrase; follow DeskAccount's official conditional recovery process."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use DeskAccount's login reset for both models because each has a password-protected interface."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Ask PhrasePocket's publisher to email the phrase after providing the receiving address."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "PhrasePocket is supplied by an interface company, so that company must retain a recoverable copy of each user's phrase."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Recovery methods depend on the stated control/access arrangement."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Compatible devices remove the need for any recovery material."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: PhrasePocket uses the protected phrase with the compatible replacement; DeskAccount uses its own official conditional account-recovery procedure."}, {"id": "KC03A-6", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Recover GuardianCircle using a phrase supplied by its publisher after checking the account name."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use GuardianCircle's configured two-of-three guardian recovery route."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Recover GuardianCircle directly through its installed interface without reaching the configured guardians."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The available guardians meet this model's stated recovery condition, not a universal rule."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Alternative recovery means conditions never matter."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The wallet label establishes a phrase fallback despite its contact-based description."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Two reachable configured guardians meet the supplied two-of-three process. This is a positive condition, not an instruction for every account."}, {"id": "KC03A-7", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Store the phrase in a searchable shared chat to preserve access after phone loss."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Send the phrase to DeskAccount support so recovery remains available when the phone is missing."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Maintain protected separated backups and private model-specific access checks."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A searchable backup label guarantees access after phone loss, so an open chat offers the same protection as a private backup."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Separation and access checks can reduce loss risk without exposing the material."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "All backups should be accessible to strangers during emergencies."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Protected separated backups and private model-specific access checks address phone loss without disclosure to chats/support. “Protected” must be explained in the reviewed lesson, not treated as a magic storage label."}, {"id": "KC03A-8", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "State that backup/device/guardian arrangements need maintenance and offer no unconditional recovery guarantee."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Promise no loss is possible after one backup is made."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Promise every provider can reset every account."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Documenting devices and recovery routes guarantees their future availability."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The three models have identical unconditional recovery."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Availability, damage, forgotten access and model conditions can still limit a plan."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Damaged/unreadable material, unavailable devices/contacts or provider conditions can still limit recovery. Maintain the plan and make no guarantee."}], "outcomes": ["O-03.1", "O-03.2", "O-03.3", "O-03.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-03-B", "canonical_id": "KC-03", "kind": "check", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-03", "title": "A backup is not always the recovery method", "fixture_html": "<p>Fixture: <strong>CounterAccount</strong> is custodial: its provider controls authorisation and offers policy-governed account recovery, but service access is unavailable during the supplied outage. <strong>LocalSeed</strong> is self-custody: its user controls authorisation; the user lost the phone and forgot its local unlock password, but has a privately stored readable recovery phrase and a compatible replacement. <strong>RecoveryTeam</strong> is an alternative account with three-of-five previously configured recovery contacts, no phrase and only two contacts currently reachable. It cannot yet meet that recovery condition. No guaranteed outcome is supplied.</p>\n<p>Placeholders: <code>DEMO-RECEIVE-ID</code> = receiving address; <code>DEMO-SPEND-KEY</code> = private key; <code>DEMO-SEED-BACKUP</code> = recovery phrase; <code>DEMO-DEVICE-PASS</code> = local unlock password; <code>DEMO-SERVICE-PASS</code> = CounterAccount login password. These are inert text. An address is not spending-secret material but can expose public activity relationships.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC03B-1", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "CounterAccount's provider controls authorisation; LocalSeed's user controls it."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Every phone owner controls their provider's network keys."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "A compatible replacement shifts LocalSeed's control to CounterAccount."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The account screen appears on the user's phone, so phone ownership determines network control even for the provider-operated account."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The supplied models assign control differently despite both using devices."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Losing a phone automatically changes the custody model."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: CounterAccount is provider-controlled; LocalSeed user-controlled. Outage/device loss does not silently change their custody models."}, {"id": "KC03B-2", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat the provider outage as permission to bypass CounterAccount through its displayed receiving address."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use LocalSeed's phrase to restore CounterAccount because both screens show the same user."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "CounterAccount needs provider availability; LocalSeed needs protected recovery access."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A phrase from one model unlocks every provider account."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Both accounts belong to the same person, so LocalSeed's recovery phrase can bypass CounterAccount's service outage and unlock its balance."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Provider availability and user-held recovery duties differ in these fixtures."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Provider service availability and private user-held recovery access impose distinct responsibilities. One account's phrase does not bypass another provider."}, {"id": "KC03B-3", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Give support the key because its name sounds like a reference."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Classify receive-ID as an address; spend-key/seed-backup as secret control/recovery material."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Classify all three as safe public identifiers."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A receiving identifier differs from the secrets that can confer control."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Any label containing DEMO proves real keys are public too."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A replacement-device recovery phrase is only a public account-reference label."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Receive-ID is an address; spend-key/seed-backup are control/recovery material. Inert fixture labels do not imply real keys can be public."}, {"id": "KC03B-4", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat the forgotten device password as mandatory even though the supplied phrase remains readable."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Share the service password with support because CounterAccount already delegates network authorisation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Protect both passwords and distinguish local unlock from provider login."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Provider passwords are public because custody is delegated."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Passwords have different access functions and remain secret."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Both interfaces ask for passwords, so the provider-login password can replace LocalSeed's phrase and restore control on any compatible device."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Local-device unlocking and provider-login access differ and both remain secret. A lost local password is not universal proof a protected phrase cannot work."}, {"id": "KC03B-5", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use LocalSeed's protected phrase; follow CounterAccount's official route when available."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Ask CounterAccount to reconstruct LocalSeed's phrase from its receiving address and user account record."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Restore LocalSeed by importing its receiving address without the protected phrase on the replacement device."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The address identifies the ledger balance and therefore supplies spending authority."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Custodial providers can reset every self-custody key."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The stated phrase route can work without the old device password; provider recovery is separate and conditional."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: The readable phrase and compatible replacement support LocalSeed recovery under the fixture. CounterAccount's official process is separate and currently constrained by availability."}, {"id": "KC03B-6", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Start RecoveryTeam recovery with two genuine contacts and defer its third-contact condition until later."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Restore a third configured contact before this recovery condition can be met."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Ask RecoveryTeam's publisher for a phrase fallback because the configured contacts cannot meet the threshold."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Two of five does not meet the supplied three-of-five rule; no fallback is stated."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The two reachable contacts are genuine and previously configured, so their identity verification makes the stated third-contact requirement optional."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every alternative model permits a universal password reset."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Two contacts do not satisfy three-of-five. Restore sufficient configured contact availability before asserting recovery through that process."}, {"id": "KC03B-7", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Maintain protected separate LocalSeed backups, private access checks and configured contact availability."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep LocalSeed's backup in a searchable shared document and publish RecoveryTeam identities for faster emergency access."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Keep LocalSeed's only backup on the replacement phone and depend on RecoveryTeam's existing two contacts without maintenance."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Public searchable backups adequately protect both phrase and contact models."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Public disclosure has no control or privacy consequence."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Separate protected material and functioning configured recovery routes address these specific failure modes."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Maintain separate protected LocalSeed backups/private checks, model-specific account access and configured contacts. Neither publishing secrets nor keeping a sole copy on the lost device is an adequate plan."}, {"id": "KC03B-8", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Promise recovery despite all contacts becoming unreachable."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Promise providers can cancel all network events."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "State the plan's remaining availability/security limits rather than a guarantee."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "No plan or supplied provider policy guarantees every future recovery condition."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A plan eliminates the need for maintenance."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The replacement device is compatible with LocalSeed, so its availability eliminates the need to protect or maintain the recovery phrase."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Available protected material and recovery conditions still matter. A plan provides no universal future recovery or reversal guarantee."}], "outcomes": ["O-03.1", "O-03.2", "O-03.3", "O-03.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-04-A", "canonical_id": "KC-04", "kind": "check", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-04", "title": "Same ticker, different receiving instruction", "fixture_html": "<p>Fixture: The independently reached <strong>PortInbox</strong> deposit instructions for Mira state: network <strong>DemoNet-A</strong>, token <strong>Lumen issuer-native</strong>, representation ID <strong>DEMO-LUMEN-A</strong>, ticker LUM, full destination <strong>DEMO-MIRA-PORT-A</strong>, required memo <strong>DEMO-MEMO-17</strong>, minimum <strong>10 LUM</strong>. Sender option S1 says <strong>LUM wrapped</strong>, ID <strong>DEMO-WLUM-A</strong>, DemoNet-A. S2 says <strong>LUM issuer-native</strong>, ID <strong>DEMO-LUMEN-B</strong>, DemoNet-B. S3 says Lumen issuer-native, ID DEMO-LUMEN-A, DemoNet-A. Their address shapes look similar. A pasted destination <strong>DEMO-MILA-PORT-A</strong> differs from Mira's full destination. Another draft has the correct destination/memo but only <strong>8 LUM</strong>. Assume the independently reached instructions are the current trustworthy inputs for this exercise; actual names or address shapes are not validated real-world routes.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC04A-1", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat all LUM entries as the same accepted representation."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Identify DEMO-LUMEN-A, issuer-native on DemoNet-A, as the declared deposit representation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use the cheapest LUM entry without reading its ID."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Identity includes the supplied representation/network information, not ticker alone."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "All displayed options say LUM, so their representation IDs merely identify interface versions rather than different receiving-route assets."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Lower cost changes the asset's identity."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: PortInbox declares issuer-native DEMO-LUMEN-A on DemoNet-A. Exact supplied representation/network identity is required; ticker/icon/cost is insufficient."}, {"id": "KC04A-2", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept S1 because a wrapper is always the issuer-native token."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Rename S1 issuer-native because both say LUM."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Keep S1's wrapped ID distinct; acceptance is not declared for it."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Every wrapper has universal receiving support."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "No supplied equivalence permits substituting the wrapped representation."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Matching DemoNet-A establishes acceptance despite the different wrapped representation."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Wrapped DEMO-WLUM-A is distinct and not declared equivalent. Same-network/token-label appearance cannot supply acceptance."}, {"id": "KC04A-3", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause S2: DemoNet-B does not match the receiving DemoNet-A route."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept S2 because the ticker matches."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept S2 if its fee is lower."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Lower fees guarantee cross-network compatibility."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "S2 says issuer-native, so its issuer identity establishes compatibility even though the receiving instruction names a different network."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Exact representation/network/service support must match together."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: S2's DemoNet-B representation/network fails the DemoNet-A route. Cheap fees do not compensate."}, {"id": "KC04A-4", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept S1 and S2 from the matching address shape without checking their supplied representation/network differences."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "S3 matches declared support; address shape does not establish acceptance."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept all three options because the ticker and destination prefix are displayed consistently."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Supplied current acceptance establishes S3's combination; appearance alone does not."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "S1 and S2 use similar destination shapes, so those shapes establish the missing asset/network acceptance without a separate receiving instruction."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Choosing an interface determines all receiving support."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: S3's exact asset/network combination matches supplied current support. Similar address shapes do not validate the others."}, {"id": "KC04A-5", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Keep MILA and add the memo, using the familiar prefix to establish Mira's identity."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Correct to MIRA but omit the memo, using matching asset/network support to establish receipt."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Correct the full destination and supply the required memo."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The familiar prefix is sufficient even when the full destination differs."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The intended recipient, whole destination and required memo must match the trustworthy instruction."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Memos are optional whenever a network is selected."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Correct Mila to the independently supplied Mira full destination and supply DEMO-MEMO-17. Recipient and required detail are separate checks."}, {"id": "KC04A-6", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause the eight-LUM draft under the ten-LUM minimum."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Continue the eight-LUM draft because the independently confirmed destination meets the receiving instruction."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Continue the eight-LUM draft because matching native representation establishes an acceptable deposit amount."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The stated deposit condition remains required even after destination details match."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The full destination points to the right recipient, so the service can credit eight LUM despite its stated ten-LUM minimum."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every service credits every positive amount