>DEMO-HARBOR-A</strong>, DemoNet-A. R2 says <strong>wrapped HBR</strong>, ID <strong>DEMO-WHBR-B</strong>, DemoNet-B. R3 says issuer-native HBR ID DEMO-HARBOR-B, DemoNet-B. All displayed address prefixes resemble one another. A recent independent recipient confirmation supplies DEMO-NIA-COVE-B; the draft uses <strong>DEMO-NINA-COVE-B</strong>. Another otherwise consistent draft has <strong>60 HBR</strong>. These are invented exercise-only acceptance conditions.</p>", "items": [{"id": "KC04B-1", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Identify DEMO-HARBOR-B, issuer-native on DemoNet-B, as the declared representation."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat every HBR label as identical."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Choose the asset solely by its icon."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The familiar HBR icon appears in the sending interface, so it uniquely identifies the recipient's exact network-specific representation."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Names/tickers cannot replace the supplied exact representation/network identity."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every deployment with the same ticker has universal deposit support."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: CoveLedger declares issuer-native DEMO-HARBOR-B on DemoNet-B. Apply this form's identity rather than memorising A's network."}, {"id": "KC04B-2", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use R2 because the network matches."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use R2 because wrapped means provider-approved."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Do not substitute DEMO-WHBR-B for the declared issuer-native ID."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Same-network wrapping preserves every native representation's receiving-service acceptance condition."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "All network-compatible tokens share one ID."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The instructions establish one representation, not equivalence to the wrapper."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: DEMO-WHBR-B is not the declared native representation; no equivalence has been supplied."}, {"id": "KC04B-3", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept R1 because issuer-native wording overrides network mismatch."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Pause R1 because DemoNet-A is not the supplied receiving network."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept R1 if a similar destination prefix is visible."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Receiving support must include the selected network and exact representation."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Any native asset is supported on every receiving network."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "R1 uses a similar destination prefix, so that visible prefix supplies the service acceptance missing from its DemoNet-A selection."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: R1's DemoNet-A selection fails the current DemoNet-B receiving route despite issuer-native wording or similar prefix."}, {"id": "KC04B-4", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "R3 matches declared asset/network support; similar prefixes do not validate R1/R2."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Every similar prefix validates all options."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "None can be supported because B previously used DemoNet-A."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The earlier form established DemoNet-A support for a native token, so that remembered network rule overrides this form's receiving instructions."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Use this independently supplied acceptance record, not an address-shape shortcut."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Network names alone establish every asset representation."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: R3 satisfies supplied asset/network support; appearance does not establish the same for R1/R2."}, {"id": "KC04B-5", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Add a memo from the earlier form to compensate for the differing recipient spelling."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep NINA because the similar prefix and selected network establish the intended recipient."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Correct the full destination to NIA; this route needs no memo."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "No-memo routes permit a wrong recipient address."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "An added memo repairs NINA/NIA even in the no-memo route."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Full destination and actual stated requirements matter; this route explicitly needs no memo."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Correct NINA to independently confirmed NIA. The actual route requires no memo; an invented memo cannot repair a wrong recipient."}, {"id": "KC04B-6", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Continue the 60-HBR draft because more is safer."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Pause/revise under the independently stated 5–50-HBR condition."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat the upper bound as optional because R3 is supported."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A supported asset does not cancel the route's stated amount condition."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Every maximum is a marketing suggestion."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The destination and native ID match the instruction, so the service must accept sixty HBR even though its stated range ends at fifty."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Sixty exceeds the supplied five-to-fifty-HBR condition. Pause/revise the draft under the stated instruction."}, {"id": "KC04B-7", "outcomes": ["O-04.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "With corrected R3 and twenty HBR, continue to the remaining transfer review."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "With corrected R3 and twenty HBR, authorise immediately because support proves the whole review complete."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "With corrected R3 and twenty HBR, keep compatibility unknown until a memo from A is added."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Correct compatibility establishes every remaining transfer fee and completion condition."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Recognise established route details and continue only the appropriate next review step."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every scenario must be paused forever to pass."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: With R3, correct destination and twenty HBR, this compatibility stage is established. Move to the remaining transfer review rather than authorising a real transfer or pretending all details are still unknown."}], "outcomes": ["O-04.1", "O-04.2", "O-04.3", "O-04.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-01-A", "canonical_id": "PM-01", "kind": "mission", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-01", "title": "Choose the route for the actual need", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-01.1–O-01.4. This is a fictional comparison; it does not request a purchase or transfer.</p>\n<p><strong>Case Local:</strong> Sade's priority is an accessible local payment with little setup and a stated dispute channel. A familiar route is available to both parties, costs 1 DEMO-CASH, keeps its records with the provider and offers conditional dispute handling without a refund guarantee. The alternative has Sade use the <strong>ClearWindow interface</strong> to authorise <strong>BTC on Bitcoin</strong>; the ledger records the event and the fictional receiving service <strong>NorthDesk</strong> applies separate credit checks. That route costs 4 DEMO-CASH equivalent, requires additional setup, exposes the described ledger event publicly and gives no reversal guarantee.</p>\n<p><strong>Case Remote:</strong> Kola's priority is reaching a recipient today. The familiar route is unavailable to that recipient, despite a 1-DEMO-CASH quote, private provider records and conditional disputes. The available classroom alternative uses <strong>TokenWindow</strong> to authorise <strong>DEMO-RIVER token on Ethereum</strong>, with the fixture's Ethereum fee paid in ETH; <strong>EastDesk</strong> separately credits its own account after checks. Setup and receiving-route details have already been checked for this comparison. Cost is 3 DEMO-CASH equivalent; the described network event is public; reversal is not guaranteed. The token's declared identity differs from ETH. Assume these invented conditions are internally consistent; no actual token deployment or service is asserted.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM01A-1", "outcomes": ["O-01.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Local: asset BTC; ledger Bitcoin; interface ClearWindow; service NorthDesk."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Local: asset ClearWindow; ledger NorthDesk; interface Bitcoin; service BTC."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Local: asset NorthDesk; ledger ClearWindow; interface BTC; service Bitcoin."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The asset and receiving-service balance appear in one interface, so ClearWindow and NorthDesk must be the same authoritative shared ledger."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The case explicitly assigns different asset/network/interface/service roles."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A service name determines which native asset it controls."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Local's asset/network/interface/service are BTC/Bitcoin/ClearWindow/NorthDesk. All four roles must match."}, {"id": "PM01A-2", "outcomes": ["O-01.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Remote: asset ETH; ledger EastDesk; interface Ethereum; service TokenWindow."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Remote: asset TokenWindow; ledger DEMO-RIVER; interface EastDesk; service Ethereum."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Remote: asset DEMO-RIVER; ledger Ethereum; interface TokenWindow; service EastDesk."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The token's record is on the supplied network; the interface and service are separate components."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The stated native fee asset must also be the transferred token."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Provider credit makes the provider itself a blockchain."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Remote's roles are DEMO-RIVER/Ethereum/TokenWindow/EastDesk; ETH's fee role does not make it the transferred token."}, {"id": "PM01A-3", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Opening ClearWindow proves NorthDesk credit."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Sade authorises; network participants process/record; NorthDesk checks and credits separately."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "NorthDesk credit necessarily authorises Sade's first request."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "ClearWindow lets Sade authorise a request, so pressing its button independently establishes network completion and NorthDesk's later receiving credit."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Service accounts must always update before permission."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Authorisation, network processing and receiving accounting are distinct responsibilities."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Sender authorisation, network processing/recording and provider credit checks have distinct participants and stages."}, {"id": "PM01A-4", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "EastDesk's update is internal accounting, not automatically another on-chain transfer."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "EastDesk's update creates a new token network because the recipient now sees a service balance."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "EastDesk's update replaces Ethereum's record because the receiving provider has completed its own accounting."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Each internal token-account update necessarily creates another blockchain record."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A service's account record can change separately from the ledger event it relies on."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A provider controls deletion of all public ledger events."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: EastDesk's account update is service accounting; it is not automatically another on-chain action or deletion of the existing ledger event."}, {"id": "PM01A-5", "outcomes": ["O-01.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "BTC identifies Ethereum's interface in Local because both cases involve a wallet service."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "BTC and DEMO-RIVER are interchangeable once an app displays the requested receiving amount."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Local uses native BTC; Remote uses a distinct issued token."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Asset/network identities come from the supplied descriptions, not a shared crypto label."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Both cases use crypto interfaces, so Remote's issued DEMO-RIVER token must have the same native-asset role as Bitcoin's BTC."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "App names prove native-asset equivalence."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: BTC is Bitcoin's native asset in Local; Remote's issued token is distinct. A common interface category does not supply interchangeability."}, {"id": "PM01A-6", "outcomes": ["O-01.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "ETH becomes DEMO-RIVER when the provider records token credit after the fee is paid."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "ETH has the stated native-fee role; DEMO-RIVER is the transferred token."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "BTC covers the stated Ethereum fee because both route descriptions involve a native crypto asset."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Local's BTC must also cover Remote's stated Ethereum fee."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A token's ticker changes the native asset."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Transferred asset and stated network fee asset can have distinct roles."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: ETH pays the supplied Ethereum fee; DEMO-RIVER is the transferred token. Do not silently merge the units or roles."}, {"id": "PM01A-7", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Choose Local's familiar route for the stated priorities; reject any guaranteed-refund claim."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Choose Local's token route because its higher fee guarantees recovery."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Choose Local's token route because public records guarantee privacy."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Compare cost, access, setup, visibility and the conditional dispute/recovery limits actually supplied."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Paying more guarantees reversal and makes public information private."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Local's familiar provider has a stated dispute channel and private records, so those conditions establish a guaranteed refund for every disputed payment."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Local's familiar route fits the declared access/setup/cost priorities and conditional disputes. Reject guaranteed recovery and public-record-anonymity claims."}, {"id": "PM01A-8", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Choose Remote's unavailable familiar route because it is cheaper."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Decline every token route regardless of recipient access."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Choose the available token route for Remote, conditionally accepting its cost/privacy/recovery limits."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Available recipient access after setup establishes guaranteed completion and recovery rights."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The stated need/access changes the best fit; no recovery guarantee follows."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A familiar route is always available once its quote is known."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Remote's recipient cannot use the familiar route. The available token comparison fits conditionally with its supplied costs and visibility/recovery limits; no actual authorisation follows."}], "outcomes": ["O-01.1", "O-01.2", "O-01.3", "O-01.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-01-B", "canonical_id": "PM-01", "kind": "mission", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-01", "title": "A different priority produces a different choice", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-01.1–O-01.4.</p>\n<p><strong>Case Reach:</strong> Femi needs a route the remote recipient can access. A familiar service costs 2 DEMO-CASH, has private provider records and conditional recovery but is unavailable to that recipient. The available token route has Femi use <strong>BridgeView</strong> to authorise <strong>DEMO-MARSH on Ethereum</strong>; ETH pays the stated network fee; <strong>WestDesk</strong> credits its account after separate checks. The token route costs 4 DEMO-CASH equivalent, has already completed its extra setup and current receiving checks, exposes the described network event publicly and has no guaranteed reversal.</p>\n<p><strong>Case Nearby:</strong> Nene prioritises low setup, a usable local route and a dispute channel. A familiar route is available to both parties, costs 1 DEMO-CASH and has private provider records with conditional disputes. The alternative uses <strong>NativeView</strong>, <strong>BTC on Bitcoin</strong>, and receiving service <strong>SouthDesk</strong> after its checks; it costs 5 DEMO-CASH equivalent, needs extra setup, makes the stated network event public and offers no reversal guarantee. No quoted price is current market data.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM01B-1", "outcomes": ["O-01.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Reach: asset BridgeView; ledger WestDesk; interface Ethereum; service DEMO-MARSH."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Reach: asset DEMO-MARSH; ledger Ethereum; interface BridgeView; service WestDesk."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Reach: asset WestDesk; ledger BridgeView; interface DEMO-MARSH; service Ethereum."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Provider credit implies the provider is the token."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Displaying token and network makes BridgeView the authoritative shared ledger."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The fixture separately names the asset, its ledger, interface and receiving account service."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Reach's asset/network/interface/service are DEMO-MARSH/Ethereum/BridgeView/WestDesk. All four roles are required."}, {"id": "PM01B-2", "outcomes": ["O-01.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Nearby: asset BTC; ledger Bitcoin; interface NativeView; service SouthDesk."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Nearby: asset NativeView; ledger SouthDesk; interface BTC; service Bitcoin."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Nearby: asset Bitcoin; ledger BTC; interface SouthDesk; service NativeView."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A service's marketing name determines the ledger."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Read the role assigned to each component in Nearby's description."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "BTC appears in NativeView's screen, so it identifies the user interface rather than the transferred native asset described in Nearby."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Nearby's roles are BTC/Bitcoin/NativeView/SouthDesk. A displayed asset is not itself a user interface."}, {"id": "PM01B-3", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "WestDesk's internal credit establishes the earlier authorisation before any network processing needs checking."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Opening BridgeView completes network processing and WestDesk credit because the recipient is accessible."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Femi authorises; network processing and later service credit remain distinct."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Different participants perform the described stages; one displayed step does not establish all later outcomes."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The accessible-recipient request screen establishes completed network processing and service credit."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Network records and provider accounts are always one database."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Femi's authorisation is followed by distinct network and service activities. One screen does not establish every later record."}, {"id": "PM01B-4", "outcomes": ["O-01.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "SouthDesk's account update must replace Bitcoin's record."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "SouthDesk can credit its account separately from the network event."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "SouthDesk's credit necessarily creates new BTC."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "An internal BTC credit necessarily issues new network-native BTC."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Account balances are always authorisation requests."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "An internal balance update has its own accounting role, not automatically a new ledger transfer."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: SouthDesk can update its own account record without that update necessarily being new BTC issuance or another network transfer."}, {"id": "PM01B-5", "outcomes": ["O-01.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Reach's transferred token is DEMO-MARSH, distinct from ETH's stated fee role."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Reach's token becomes BTC because it can be received."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Every token is Ethereum's native ETH."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A receiving service makes every asset native to the same network."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Read token identity separately from the network's native fee asset."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The fee and transfer appear in one interface, so DEMO-MARSH must be the same native asset as the ETH used for fees."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: DEMO-MARSH is the transferred token; Ethereum's stated ETH fee role is separate."}, {"id": "PM01B-6", "outcomes": ["O-01.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Nearby's BTC is an Ethereum token."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Nearby's BTC and Reach's ETH are the same native asset."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "BTC is native to Bitcoin; ETH belongs to Ethereum's stated native-fee role."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "These network/asset roles differ, despite both being crypto assets."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Both BTC and ETH are native assets in these cases, so either can be substituted on whichever network the interface selects."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Paying a fee changes an asset's issuer/network identity."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Bitcoin/BTC and Ethereum/ETH retain distinct native roles in the supplied cases. Neither native nor crypto establishes universal support."}, {"id": "PM01B-7", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Choose Reach's familiar route regardless of its unavailability."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Choose Reach's available token route conditionally, without promising recovery."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Choose the token route because its public record guarantees anonymity."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Access alone establishes guaranteed reversal."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Reach's token quote is higher than its familiar quote, so the extra cost establishes stronger consumer protection and a reversal guarantee."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Reach's access priority is met; cost, visibility and recovery limits remain."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Reach's available token route fits its access priority while retaining cost, public-event and recovery limits. No guarantee is created by access."}, {"id": "PM01B-8", "outcomes": ["O-01.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Choose Nearby's familiar route for stated priorities, while treating dispute handling as conditional."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Choose Nearby's BTC route because every crypto transfer has guaranteed recovery."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Reject the familiar route because provider records can never support disputes."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "An accessible familiar route with disputes guarantees every disputed refund."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Its access, setup, cost and stated dispute route fit; no unconditional guarantee is supplied."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Public ledger visibility is necessarily more private than provider records."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Nearby's familiar route fits the stated local priorities. A conditional dispute channel is useful but not an unconditional refund promise."}], "outcomes": ["O-01.1", "O-01.2", "O-01.3", "O-01.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-02-A", "canonical_id": "PM-02", "kind": "mission", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-02", "title": "Triage a fictional inbox", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-02.1–O-02.4. No actual inbox, link or wallet is used.</p>\n<p><strong>Message Pressure:</strong> a copied <strong>CanalAccount</strong> logo, “Your account closes in five minutes; pay 6 DEMO-CASH first to unlock a guaranteed 40% gain.” Sender route: <code>DEMO-PRESSURE-LINK</code>. <strong>Message Support:</strong> “Send your recovery phrase to verify access.” <strong>Message Permission:</strong> “Free receipt check,” but the authority panel gives an unrelated spender unlimited DEMO-TOKEN spending. <strong>Message Maintenance:</strong> an ordinary account-maintenance announcement. You independently use your previously known bookmark to reach the mock support panel: it confirms the maintenance notice and says it requests no payment, secrets or permissions; it does not confirm the gain offer. Do not reuse the purported sender's link or a sponsored result.</p>\n<p><strong>Receipt R1:</strong> sender screenshot, 17 DEMO-TOKEN paid; independently opened recipient account says Pending, reference DEMO-R1, no credited balance. <strong>Receipt R2:</strong> independently opened recipient account says Credited, 9 DEMO-TOKEN, matching reference DEMO-R2 and intended recipient. No separate local bank/mobile-money payout record is present.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM02A-1", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pay the advance charge after checking the branded deadline to preserve the stated gain."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Stop the request; identify its deadline, guarantee and advance charge."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept the gain after checking its exact percentage against the message's countdown and copied logo."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Urgency and unsupported gains plus an advance charge warrant stopping and independent verification."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "An exact percentage guarantees the outcome."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A short branded countdown establishes regulatory approval of the promised gain."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Stop the pressured guaranteed-gain/advance-charge request; identify the actual deadline, promise and charge rather than paying to test it."}, {"id": "PM02A-2", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The familiar logo independently establishes the sender."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Paying first verifies the sender's identity."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Copied branding is compatible with impersonation; the sender remains unverified."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "No genuine message ever contains branding."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Branding can be copied and is not independent identity evidence."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The release charge is paid before the promised gain, so payment successfully reaching the sender would establish its account ownership and genuine identity."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Copied branding can support impersonation and does not independently establish the claimed sender."}, {"id": "PM02A-3", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use the previously known bookmark to reach mock support."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use DEMO-PRESSURE-LINK to reach the branded account page and ask it to verify the sender."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use a sponsored logo-matching result to reach support because its position confirms identity."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "DEMO-PRESSURE-LINK opens a familiar-looking account page, so asking support there is independent verification once the user reaches the page privately."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Advertisements establish service ownership."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Independently chosen known support avoids depending on the message channel."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Use the previously known bookmark to the mock account support; sender links/ads are not independent verification."}, {"id": "PM02A-4", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept the gain offer as well because genuine account support confirmed a same-brand notice."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Confirm Maintenance only; keep the unrelated gain offer unverified."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Reject Maintenance despite its independent confirmation because the copied-brand gain offer was suspicious."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Verification applies to the particular claim checked, not every claim using the same brand."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A confirmed same-brand maintenance notice also substantiates the separate gain offer."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Independent support can never confirm a legitimate notice."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Genuine independent support confirms Maintenance only. Do not extend that confirmation to the gain offer, or refuse a confirmed ordinary notice solely by association."}, {"id": "PM02A-5", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Give the phrase to the claimed support representative."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Give only several words to the representative."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Refuse the recovery-material request; use only model-appropriate private recovery processes."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The requester labels the phrase a support verification field, so its disclosed words no longer carry the spending-control significance of recovery material."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Recovery material can confer control and should not be disclosed to external requesters."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every partial phrase disclosure is harmless."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Refuse the outside phrase request; protect control material and use only the relevant model's private recovery process. No real secret is requested."}, {"id": "PM02A-6", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Refuse Permission's unexplained unlimited authority to an unrelated spender."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept because the fee is zero."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept because no phrase is requested."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Secret disclosure is the only consequential action."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Free receipt-check wording establishes harmlessness despite the stated spending authority."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Actual authority matters even without revealing a phrase or showing a fee."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Refuse the unexplained outsider spending permission. A free/receipt/phrase-free label does not remove its stated consequences."}, {"id": "PM02A-7", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Fulfil R1 because the screenshot says paid."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep R1 receipt unconfirmed and check the independent receiving status/reference."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Declare R1 permanently lost because it is Pending."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Pending receiving evidence is not credit; a screenshot neither establishes receipt nor permanent loss."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The sender screenshot contains a payment amount and reference, so it supplies better receiving evidence than the recipient's still-Pending account record."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every delay proves a permanent loss."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: R1 is Pending, not credited. Obtain current matched receiving evidence; neither deliver on the screenshot nor assume permanent loss."}, {"id": "PM02A-8", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat R2 as no credit because R1 is Pending."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat R2 as local payout completed."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Recognise R2's matched account credit; local payout remains unconfirmed."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Matching token credit necessarily proves arrival in the separate local account."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The independent R2 record establishes its credit, not another reference or payout."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "One pending transaction prevents every later credit."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: R2's independent matched record establishes nine-token credit for R2. A separate payout remains unconfirmed; R1 is a different claim."}], "outcomes": ["O-02.1", "O-02.2", "O-02.3", "O-02.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-02-B", "canonical_id": "PM-02", "kind": "mission", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-02", "title": "Separate a genuine update from a different request", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-02.1–O-02.4.</p>\n<p><strong>Offer Update:</strong> a claimed <strong>FerryService</strong> administrator uses copied branding: “Guaranteed 25% daily yield; the slot expires tonight. Send a 3-DEMO-CASH activation fee through <code>DEMO-OFFER-LINK</code>.” <strong>Key Request:</strong> “Upload your private key as a support reference.” <strong>Sign Request:</strong> a “zero-cost login” panel gives spender DEMO-OUTSIDER spending authority over all DEMO-UNIT; no purpose is explained. <strong>Service Update:</strong> an ordinary scheduled maintenance notice. You independently reach FerryService through a previously known account route. Its support view confirms the maintenance notice and requests no payment, secret or signature; it does not confirm the yield offer. An attractive search advert repeats the offer's wording but supplies no independent verification.</p>\n<p><strong>Receipt S1:</strong> a sender screenshot claims 14 DEMO-UNIT, reference DEMO-S1. Your independent receiving view supplies no matching credit; it lists an unrelated credit DEMO-OTHER for 4 units. <strong>Receipt S2:</strong> your independent receiving view says Credited, 14 DEMO-UNIT, matching DEMO-S2 and recipient. A separate independent local payout view says <strong>Processing</strong>, not Paid. These records do not supply a universal payout time.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM02B-1", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Stop the yield/activation request; identify guarantee, deadline and advance charge."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Send the advance fee after checking the precise rate and matching brand in the message."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat the short deadline as evidence the account administrator has independently approved the yield."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Agreement between precise yield, deadline and fee independently proves the return."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Deadline pressure and an advance charge do not establish a guaranteed return."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every service notice promises the same yield."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Unsupported yield, deadline and advance activation fee warrant stopping/verifying; precise numbers are not proof."}, {"id": "PM02B-2", "outcomes": ["O-02.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The logo proves the administrator controls your account."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "A matching advert independently verifies the administrator."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat copied identity/advert wording as unverified, potentially impersonated claims."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Similar graphics and repetition are not independent identity evidence."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The matching branded offer appears as a sponsored search result, so paid placement independently establishes that the representative is authorised by FerryService."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every genuine provider uses activation fees for guaranteed yield."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Repeated/copied branding and advert wording do not independently establish the administrator's identity."}, {"id": "PM02B-3", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Open DEMO-OFFER-LINK to reach its branded support page and ask it to confirm the administrator."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use the previously known account route to genuine mock support."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use the highest sponsored same-brand result because the placement establishes service ownership."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Higher sponsored placement independently establishes service ownership and administrator identity."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Sender-controlled verification is independent."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The verification route is chosen separately from the unverified sender/advert."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Reach genuine mock support through the known separate account route. Paid search position and sender self-confirmation are insufficient."}, {"id": "PM02B-4", "outcomes": ["O-02.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Reject all updates even after independent confirmation."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Confirm the offer because maintenance is genuine."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Recognise the confirmed maintenance claim while keeping the offer unverified."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The genuine support view confirms one FerryService notice, so the shared brand establishes that the separate administrator's yield offer is also genuine."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Evidence is specific to the checked notice, not to every claimed message."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Suspicious messages prevent genuine notices existing."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Confirm only the particular maintenance notice supported by the independent view. The unrelated offer remains unverified."}, {"id": "PM02B-5", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Refuse the private-key upload to external support."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Upload it because the field calls it a reference."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Upload it if a fee is not charged."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A reference label cannot remove the key's spending-control significance."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The private-key field is described as a support reference and requests no direct payment, so entering it only verifies the account identity."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "No charge makes secret disclosure reversible."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Refuse the private-key upload; a support/reference label does not change control material into receipt data."}, {"id": "PM02B-6", "outcomes": ["O-02.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Approve Sign Request because it says login."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Decline its unexplained outsider spending authority."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Approve because no transfer fee is displayed."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A login label guarantees no permissions."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "No displayed fee or immediate transfer rules out later spending consequences."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The stated permission can affect control without a private-key disclosure or visible fee."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Decline the unexplained outsider spending authority, despite a login/zero-fee label. Secret exposure and authority are different routes to consequence."}, {"id": "PM02B-7", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use DEMO-OTHER's 4-unit credit to confirm S1's 14 units."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat the screenshot alone as receiving proof."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Keep S1 unconfirmed; obtain the correct matching receiving record."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The independent receiving account contains a recent credit from the sender, so DEMO-OTHER can verify S1 without matching the stated amount and reference."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Amount/reference/recipient must match the claim; an unrelated credit is insufficient."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Missing matching credit proves permanent loss immediately."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: DEMO-OTHER's four-unit credit does not match S1's fourteen-unit reference. Keep S1 unconfirmed and obtain the actual matching evidence."}, {"id": "PM02B-8", "outcomes": ["O-02.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Recognise S2 account credit; its separate local payout remains Processing."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Call S2 Paid because provider credit is shown."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Call S2 uncredited despite the matching Credited record."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Separate independent records establish credit and the still-incomplete payout stage."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Credited and Paid are interchangeable words in all routes."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "S2's local payout is still Processing, so that unfinished later stage means the earlier matching provider-credit record cannot yet establish any credit."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: S2 is independently credited; its separate local payout is Processing. Recognise both established and uncompleted stages without claiming a time guarantee."}], "outcomes": ["O-02.1", "O-02.2", "O-02.3", "O-02.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-03-A", "canonical_id": "PM-03", "kind": "mission", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-03", "title": "Recover after a lost phone", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-03.1–O-03.4. All labels are inert placeholders; do not practise restoration of an actual account.</p>\n<p><strong>Account C:</strong> custodial <strong>AnchorDesk</strong> controls network authorisation, offers a policy-governed identity-based recovery process and currently has a functioning independently known account-support route. The user's login password is secret; the user is not given the provider's spending key. <strong>Account S:</strong> self-custody <strong>QuietSeed</strong>; its user controls spending. The phone is lost; its local unlock password only unlocks that phone. A protected readable recovery phrase was stored separately, and a compatible replacement is supplied in the mock exercise. QuietSeed's company has no phrase-reset service. <strong>Account G:</strong> an alternative model, <strong>GuardianLane</strong>, uses two of three configured recovery contacts, not a phrase; two are reachable, and the supplied guardian process is available. None guarantees success under every future condition.</p>\n<p>Mock labels: receiving address DEMO-RCV; private key DEMO-KEY-ONLY; phrase DEMO-RESTORE; local unlock password DEMO-LOCAL; provider login password DEMO-LOGIN. A “support helper” asks to receive DEMO-RESTORE and DEMO-LOGIN through a chat. Private offline labels in this exercise are not values to upload. Backups can be lost, damaged, exposed or inaccessible; contact/provider availability can change.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM03A-1", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat both C and S as user-controlled network-key accounts because each uses a phone."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat C as provider-controlled authorisation and S as user-controlled authorisation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat S as provider-controlled because its company made the interface."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Phone ownership establishes custody regardless of the account description."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The supplied control arrangements, rather than interface branding, determine responsibility."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "QuietSeed's company supplies the installed interface, so that publisher necessarily controls the network authorisation even though the user holds the recovery phrase."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: AnchorDesk controls C's network authorisation; QuietSeed's user controls S. App branding or phone possession does not decide that distinction."}, {"id": "PM03A-2", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "C depends on provider operation/policy; S requires the user's protected recovery access."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "C and S can both bypass lost access using the provider's login reset."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "S can skip backups because its balance is on a ledger."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A surviving ledger balance supplies spending authority without protected recovery access."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A provider reset restores every account on any network."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Delegated custody and user-held control create different dependencies and duties."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: C depends on provider operation/policy; S requires the user to maintain protected control/recovery access. A ledger balance alone does not supply spending authority."}, {"id": "PM03A-3", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Upload all five fields to support because receiving addresses appear in public payment records."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat the key and phrase as routine receipt identifiers once the requester calls them support references."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Distinguish public receiving information from secrets; refuse the phrase upload."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Address purpose differs from spending/recovery material; public identifiers do not make secrets public."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The mock account screen labels an address, key and phrase together, so every displayed field can be shared under the same receiving-information conditions."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Renaming a phrase as a support reference removes its control function."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Receiving address DEMO-RCV is distinct from private key/phrase. Refuse the phrase upload; public address information does not make secrets safe to share."}, {"id": "PM03A-4", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Give DEMO-LOGIN to the helper because the provider controls the network key."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep DEMO-LOCAL and DEMO-LOGIN secret; distinguish device unlock from account login."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use DEMO-LOCAL as the provider's account password."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A local password and provider login are the same recovery tool."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Delegated network custody makes the provider-login password a public account reference."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Both grant access under their distinct models and should not be disclosed to the helper."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Local unlocking and provider login are different functions; both remain protected. A helper should receive neither."}, {"id": "PM03A-5", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use S's protected phrase privately; use C's independently reached conditional recovery process."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Ask AnchorDesk to email S's phrase after identifying its receiving address; import that phrase to restore C."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Restore S from its public address; let the chat helper reset C after receiving its login password."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Either route works whenever a receiving address is known."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The fixture supports different recovery paths; neither creates a universal reset service."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "AnchorDesk offers account recovery, so it must also hold and reset the phrase associated with QuietSeed whenever the same user loses a phone."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: S's readable protected phrase plus compatible replacement supports its private recovery route; C's functioning independent official process supports conditional account recovery. Do not cross the models or upload material to a helper."}, {"id": "PM03A-6", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Ask GuardianLane's publisher for a phrase fallback so the user does not need to involve contacts."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use GuardianLane's installed interface to restore access before consulting its currently reachable configured contacts."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use GuardianLane's available two-of-three configured-contact recovery process."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Two reachable contacts meet this model's stated threshold; it is not a rule for other models."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Every alternative account has the same phrase fallback."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Knowing GuardianLane's app and address bypasses the configured-contact threshold."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Two reachable configured contacts meet GuardianLane's stated two-of-three process. No phrase/app-name bypass is supplied."}, {"id": "PM03A-7", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Move S's only phrase copy into an open shared chat; send C's login to a helper; let G's contacts lapse."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Maintain separate protected S backups and private access checks, C's official recovery access, and G's configured contact availability."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Keep S's only backup on its replacement phone; reuse C's login publicly; assume G's setup needs no review."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A shared searchable backup stays accessible after phone loss, so its convenience provides the same spending-control protection as a private separated backup."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The plan addresses device loss, secret exposure and the differing conditional recovery routes."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Provider custody and guardians remove all access-maintenance responsibilities."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Plan separately for protected/readable independent S backups, official C access and maintained G contacts. Keep secrets private and avoid sole-device copies."}, {"id": "PM03A-8", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "State remaining backup, device, provider and contact limits without guaranteeing recovery."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Promise the protected backups eliminate future access problems once a readable copy has been made separately."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Promise AnchorDesk can reverse a network loss after the user verifies identity through a support ticket."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Documenting recovery routes establishes unconditional compensation if those steps fail."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A backup removes any need to check readability or access."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A plan reduces specific risks but still depends on available and protected recovery conditions."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: Material, access, contact and service conditions remain limiting factors. A documented plan reduces identified risks without guaranteeing recovery or refunds."}], "outcomes": ["O-03.1", "O-03.2", "O-03.3", "O-03.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-03-B", "canonical_id": "PM-03", "kind": "mission", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-03", "title": "Two contacts are no longer enough", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite: none. Required outcomes: O-03.1–O-03.4.</p>\n<p><strong>Account P:</strong> custodial <strong>BeaconDesk</strong>, provider-controlled authorisation; policy-governed identity/account recovery exists but its service is temporarily offline in this fixture. Use its independently known support route when available; no bypass/reset guarantee is supplied. <strong>Account U:</strong> user-controlled <strong>PrivateSeed</strong>; the device and local password are lost, but a privately stored readable recovery phrase and a compatible replacement are available. The interface publisher cannot replace the phrase. <strong>Account R:</strong> alternative model <strong>ContactRing</strong> needs three of five preconfigured recovery contacts, no phrase. Only two are currently reachable; no fallback is supplied.</p>\n<p>Mock fields: DEMO-DEST = receiving address; DEMO-CONTROL = private spending key; DEMO-BACKUP = recovery phrase; DEMO-UNLOCK = local-device password; DEMO-ACCOUNT = provider-login password. An outside “restoration agent” offers to collect DEMO-CONTROL, DEMO-BACKUP and DEMO-ACCOUNT. No actual values or restoration are performed. The plan must address protected recovery information, replacement access, provider downtime and contact availability, with no guaranteed outcome.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM03B-1", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "P becomes self-custody during downtime; U becomes custodial after losing its phone."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Both controllers are determined by whichever app is installed now."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "P's provider controls authorisation; U's user controls it under the supplied model."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Service downtime and device loss do not themselves change the declared custody arrangement."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Losing a screen transfers its spending authority to any provider."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "BeaconDesk's service is offline, so the outage automatically gives its user direct network-key control and changes the account to self-custody."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "C: Provider downtime and a lost user device do not automatically change custody. BeaconDesk controls P, the user controls U."}, {"id": "PM03B-2", "outcomes": ["O-03.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "P requires provider availability/policy; U requires its protected recovery route."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "P can use U's phrase to bypass provider downtime."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "U needs no secret protection because it has a receiving address."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Public receiving information is sufficient for spending control."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Both accounts belong to the same user, so U's stored phrase can restore P's provider balance without waiting for the separate provider service."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The models create different provider and user-control responsibilities."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "C: P needs its provider route; U needs its protected user-held recovery access. An address or another account's phrase is not a universal bypass."}, {"id": "PM03B-3", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Upload the private key and phrase as routine receipt references."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep CONTROL/BACKUP secret; DEST is a receiving identifier, with privacy implications."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Replace every account password with DEST because it is easy to remember."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "An address is interchangeable with spending-control material."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Purpose and control consequence determine secret status; labels do not erase them."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A receiving identifier without a personal name guarantees unlinked public activity."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: DEST is receiving information with privacy implications; CONTROL and BACKUP are secret control/recovery material. Do not upload them to the agent."}, {"id": "PM03B-4", "outcomes": ["O-03.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Send ACCOUNT to the restoration agent but keep UNLOCK private."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat UNLOCK as P's provider login because both are passwords."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Protect both passwords and distinguish local unlock from provider-login access."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Both access functions should remain protected; neither is automatically a universal recovery phrase."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Provider custody removes the need to protect its login."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "U's original local password is lost, so that loss invalidates its protected phrase even though the replacement is compatible and the phrase remains readable."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Protect provider-login and local-device passwords, distinguish their functions, and do not equate a local-password loss with invalidating every phrase recovery route."}, {"id": "PM03B-5", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use U's protected phrase privately; pursue P's official conditional recovery when available."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use P's account reset to restore U's control when BeaconDesk resumes service, without using the stored phrase."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Give the restoration agent U's phrase and P's login so one procedure can bypass the current provider outage."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The shared owner means one provider-login reset restores both account models."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The available phrase route and unavailable provider route follow their own stated conditions."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Sharing a phrase makes a provider outage irrelevant for every account."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: U's phrase route is available with the supplied compatible replacement. P's official recovery remains conditional on provider availability/policy. Secret disclosure is not a supported bypass."}, {"id": "PM03B-6", "outcomes": ["O-03.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Begin R's recovery with two contacts and assume the third is optional."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Restore access to a third configured contact before this supplied recovery route can satisfy its threshold."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Ask the interface publisher for a phrase that R's model does not use."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The two reachable contacts were previously configured and are genuine, so their confirmed identities mean the three-of-five threshold can be completed later."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Every alternative account secretly uses a phrase fallback."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Two does not meet three-of-five, and no other supported route is supplied."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Two does not meet ContactRing's three-of-five threshold. Restore a third configured contact before asserting that route can satisfy its recovery conditions."}, {"id": "PM03B-7", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Keep U's only backup on the replacement device and rely on the agent; stop maintaining R contacts."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Publish U's phrase to ensure availability, and share P's login for faster support."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Maintain protected independent U backups/access checks, P's official recovery access, and R's configured contacts."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Each plan component addresses a model-specific loss/exposure/availability problem without handing secrets to others."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Publishing the phrase provides protection equivalent to private separated storage."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "All three models can use the same publicly shared recovery file."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Maintain model-specific independent protected backup/access routes and contacts rather than public/sole-device copies or agent disclosure."}, {"id": "PM03B-8", "outcomes": ["O-03.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "State remaining readability, contact and provider limits without promising recovery."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Promise recovery once the backup plan lists each account, even if contacts later become unreachable."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Promise BeaconDesk recovery during the supplied outage after checking the user's independently known receiving address."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The backup plan names devices and contacts, so writing it ensures the recovery materials remain readable and every configured contact remains reachable."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Risk reduction is conditional on material and recovery routes remaining protected and available."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Provider account recovery is a universal override of network control."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "C: Readability, protection and availability still constrain every plan; the current provider outage has no supplied guaranteed bypass."}], "outcomes": ["O-03.1", "O-03.2", "O-03.3", "O-03.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-04-A", "canonical_id": "PM-04", "kind": "mission", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-04", "title": "Catch the incompatible transfer, then recognise the corrected route", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite outcomes: <strong>O-04.1, O-04.2, O-04.3</strong>. Required mission outcomes: O-04.1–O-04.4. Reading the instructions never satisfies the gate. Approved applicable KC/challenge evidence must cover the declared prerequisites before scored use; this draft does not approve a gate or mark someone eligible.</p>\n<p><strong>Trusted instruction:</strong> Independently reached <strong>MarinaInbox</strong> for recipient Tola accepts <strong>Orbit issuer-native</strong>, ticker ORB, ID <strong>DEMO-ORB-A</strong>, network <strong>DemoNet-A</strong>, full destination <strong>DEMO-TOLA-MARINA-A</strong>, required tag <strong>DEMO-TAG-42</strong>, amount <strong>10–100 ORB</strong>. These are invented conditions.</p>\n<p><strong>Draft One:</strong> 20 ORB, <strong>wrapped</strong> ID DEMO-WORB-A, DemoNet-A, full destination DEMO-TOLA-MARINA-A, tag DEMO-TAG-42. <strong>Draft Two:</strong> 20 ORB, issuer-native ID <strong>DEMO-ORB-B</strong>, <strong>DemoNet-B</strong>, same displayed destination prefix, quoted cheaper fee. <strong>Draft Three:</strong> issuer-native DEMO-ORB-A, DemoNet-A, destination <strong>DEMO-TOMO-MARINA-A</strong>, <strong>no tag</strong>, 20 ORB. <strong>Draft Four:</strong> correct native ID/network/full destination/tag, <strong>5 ORB</strong>. <strong>Corrected Draft:</strong> 20 ORB, issuer-native DEMO-ORB-A, DemoNet-A, full destination DEMO-TOLA-MARINA-A, DEMO-TAG-42; all current compatibility/destination/deposit conditions above match. Amount/fee/authorisation review is the next separate exercise. A separate <strong>Unknown Draft</strong> says ORB and a familiar address shape but leaves representation/network support unstated.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM04A-1", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use the ORB label to identify any candidate displayed by the same receiving interface."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Identify issuer-native DEMO-ORB-A on DemoNet-A as the declared representation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Choose DEMO-WORB-A after comparing its lower cost and matching destination against the native option."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Fees determine which token representation the receiver accepts."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "All candidates display ORB inside the same sending interface, so the ticker proves their representation IDs are equivalent for MarinaInbox deposits."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The supplied exact representation/network information distinguishes the accepted asset."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: MarinaInbox declares issuer-native DEMO-ORB-A on DemoNet-A. Ticker/icon/cost cannot replace exact identity."}, {"id": "PM04A-2", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause Draft One: the wrapped representation is not declared equivalent."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept Draft One after matching its ticker/network to the native instruction, ignoring the different representation ID."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept Draft One after matching its recipient/tag to the instruction, treating those fields as representation evidence."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Network/destination matches cannot establish unstated representation equivalence."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Any wrapped asset is the issuer-native asset by definition."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Draft One has the correct destination and tag, so those recipient fields establish acceptance even when its wrapped representation differs from the declared native ID."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Draft One's wrapper is distinct and not supported by a declared equivalence. Matching network/destination/tag cannot repair representation mismatch."}, {"id": "PM04A-3", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept Draft Two because it is cheaper."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept Draft Two because its destination prefix looks familiar."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Pause Draft Two; the selected network/representation combination is unsupported by this instruction."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The cheaper quote and familiar prefix establish cross-network receiving support."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Exact selected network and asset/service support must match; neither cost nor address shape supplies it."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Prefix similarity provides the missing network acceptance."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Draft Two uses an unsupported DemoNet-B representation/network combination. Cheap fees and similar prefixes do not establish acceptance."}, {"id": "PM04A-4", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat Unknown Draft as supported from its ORB ticker/address shape."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep Unknown Draft unresolved and check exact representation/network against current independent receiving instructions."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Borrow Draft Two's network because its quote is cheap."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Ticker plus prefix determines every receiving condition."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Draft Two lists a network and low fee, so those supplied offer details can fill Unknown Draft's missing support fields without another receiving check."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Missing exact support information needs its own receiving-route check."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Unknown Draft lacks exact support information. Independently check representation and selected network against current receiving instructions rather than filling fields from another offer."}, {"id": "PM04A-5", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Resolve Draft Three to Tola's full destination and required tag from the independently supplied instruction."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep TOMO and add the tag, assuming a matching prefix identifies Tola."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Correct to TOLA but omit the tag, assuming network matching is enough."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Both intended full destination and the required tag must match; one correction cannot replace the other."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A correct required tag compensates for the independently mismatched full destination."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A correct network makes recipient details optional."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Resolve TOMO/TOLA full destination and include the independently specified tag. Both must match; neither can compensate for the other."}, {"id": "PM04A-6", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Continue Draft Four because every positive amount qualifies."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Pause/revise Draft Four under the supplied 10–100-ORB deposit rule."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Continue Draft Four because its destination and tag match."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Draft Four correctly identifies Tola's destination and tag, so those matches cancel MarinaInbox's amount condition and require it to credit five ORB."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Five ORB is below the explicit minimum despite correct identity/destination details."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "A service must credit any amount using the accepted network."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Draft Four is below the explicit ten-ORB minimum. Correct destination/tag/asset does not waive the amount condition."}, {"id": "PM04A-7", "outcomes": ["O-04.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Submit Corrected Draft immediately because the independent receiving conditions match and no mismatch remains in this stage."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Keep its compatibility unknown because A's earlier drafts contained mismatched representations, destinations or amounts."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Recognise established compatibility and continue to the remaining transfer review."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Current compatibility also establishes all later fee, authorisation and processing requirements."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The corrected fixture establishes this stage; it does not substitute for the remaining transfer review."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Every practice case must be rejected even when complete."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Corrected Draft establishes the declared compatibility/destination/deposit stage. Proceed only to the remaining transfer review, not real authorisation or a guaranteed result."}, {"id": "PM04A-8", "outcomes": ["O-04.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause Unknown Draft and obtain the missing current support information."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Infer its asset/network support from the cheapest named offer and move directly to the authorisation stage."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Reject all future routes after this incomplete offer rather than checking the current receiving instruction."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A named coin ensures universal support."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The cheapest named offer verifies Unknown Draft's missing receiving-support policy."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Proportionate verification addresses the actual gap without inventing compatibility or permanent failure."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Pause the specific unresolved compatibility decision and obtain the exact missing independent support information; do not invent support or a permanent all-route failure."}], "outcomes": ["O-04.1", "O-04.2", "O-04.3", "O-04.4"], "prerequisites": ["O-04.1", "O-04.2", "O-04.3"], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-04-B", "canonical_id": "PM-04", "kind": "mission", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-04", "title": "A no-tag route is still a precise route", "fixture_html": "<p>Proposed prerequisite outcomes: <strong>O-04.1, O-04.2, O-04.3</strong>. Required mission outcomes: O-04.1–O-04.4. The same gate boundary as A applies.</p>\n<p><strong>Trusted instruction:</strong> Independently reached <strong>DuneAccount</strong> for Esi accepts <strong>Harbor issuer-native</strong>, ticker HBR, ID <strong>DEMO-HBR-B</strong>, network <strong>DemoNet-B</strong>, full destination <strong>DEMO-ESI-DUNE-B</strong>, <strong>no tag required</strong>, amount <strong>5–40 HBR</strong>. These invented route conditions replace A's; do not carry A's network/tag rule into B.</p>\n<p><strong>Draft Red:</strong> 12 HBR, <strong>wrapped</strong> ID DEMO-WHBR-B, DemoNet-B, correct destination. <strong>Draft Blue:</strong> issuer-native ID <strong>DEMO-HBR-A</strong>, <strong>DemoNet-A</strong>, similar displayed address prefix, lower quoted fee. <strong>Draft Green:</strong> native DEMO-HBR-B, DemoNet-B, destination <strong>DEMO-ESIE-DUNE-B</strong>, 12 HBR, no tag. <strong>Draft Gold:</strong> correct native ID/network/full destination, no tag, <strong>45 HBR</strong>. <strong>Corrected Draft:</strong> native DEMO-HBR-B, DemoNet-B, full destination DEMO-ESI-DUNE-B, no tag, 12 HBR; the current compatibility/destination/deposit conditions match. Next comes the remaining amount/fee/authorisation review. <strong>Unresolved Draft:</strong> native-sounding HBR name, network unstated, representation ID missing, similar address shape; no independent support record establishes it.</p>", "items": [{"id": "PM04B-1", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use any HBR entry because the icon matches."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Pick the cheapest HBR deployment as the receiving asset."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Identify issuer-native DEMO-HBR-B on DemoNet-B as the declared receiving representation."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The exact supplied identity/network defines this route; a ticker or icon is insufficient."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "The lowest-cost HBR deployment appears in the same interface, so the cheaper offer independently establishes DuneAccount's acceptance of that network-specific representation."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Native and wrapped assets are interchangeable in every deposit route."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: DuneAccount declares issuer-native DEMO-HBR-B on DemoNet-B. Apply the current form's exact identity, not A's network or an icon shortcut."}, {"id": "PM04B-2", "outcomes": ["O-04.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Accept Red after matching its network and destination, treating the wrapper label as interface wording."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Pause Red: its wrapped ID is not the declared native representation."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Rename Red issuer-native after matching its HBR ticker to the trusted instruction and keeping its existing ID."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Same-network appearance guarantees representation equivalence."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Red identifies the intended destination and DemoNet-B, so those matching fields establish acceptance despite its wrapped ID differing from the native instruction."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "No supplied equivalence establishes acceptance of the wrapper."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Red's wrapper differs from the declared issuer-native representation and has no supplied acceptance equivalence."}, {"id": "PM04B-3", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause Blue because its DemoNet-A representation/network does not match this DemoNet-B receiving route."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept Blue because issuer-native means supported everywhere."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept Blue because its fee is lower and address shape is similar."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Blue's destination prefix looks like Esi's current destination, so that appearance establishes service acceptance even though the selected representation is on DemoNet-A."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Identity, selected network and current service acceptance must match together."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Native wording cancels the network requirement."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Blue's DemoNet-A combination does not match this DemoNet-B route. Lower cost/native wording/address shape do not supply support."}, {"id": "PM04B-4", "outcomes": ["O-04.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat Unresolved Draft as supported because A used a similar name."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Borrow DemoNet-A from Blue to fill the missing field."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Obtain exact representation/network support from the independent current receiving instruction."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Blue provides a complete native-asset offer, so its network details can fill Unresolved Draft's missing network and representation fields without independent receiving evidence."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "A prior form's network rule automatically applies."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Address shape and native-sounding names cannot establish the missing acceptance."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: Missing network/ID/support needs current independent receiving instructions. A familiar name or other offer is not a substitute."}, {"id": "PM04B-5", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Keep ESIE and add A's tag, treating that tag as sufficient to identify the intended recipient."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Correct Green to the full ESI destination; follow its no-tag instruction."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Keep ESIE after matching the similar prefix and current network, treating the remaining spelling difference as harmless."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Intended recipient/full destination must match; inventing a tag does not repair a wrong destination."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Adding A's tag redirects ESIE to Esi despite the destination mismatch."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "Similar recipient spelling proves that the full destination is equivalent."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Resolve ESIE to the independently supplied ESI full destination. This route explicitly requires no tag; inventing A's tag cannot redirect a wrong destination."}, {"id": "PM04B-6", "outcomes": ["O-04.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause/revise Gold to meet the explicit 5–40-HBR condition."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Accept Gold because higher amounts improve acceptance."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Accept Gold because native identity cancels the upper bound."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "A current native deployment has no provider amount conditions."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Forty-five HBR exceeds the supplied maximum despite correct route details."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "The provider labels its amount maximum beside the fee information, so the forty-HBR upper bound can be treated as a fee estimate rather than a deposit condition."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "2", "feedback": "E: Forty-five HBR exceeds the supplied forty-HBR maximum. Pause/revise under this route's current acceptance condition."}, {"id": "PM04B-7", "outcomes": ["O-04.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Call Corrected Draft incompatible until A's tag is supplied despite this route's explicit no-tag condition."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Authorise immediately because the current compatibility/destination/deposit conditions establish every later transfer detail."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Recognise established compatibility and continue to the remaining transfer review."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "Every receiving route requires A's tag regardless of its own instructions."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Corrected Draft matches DuneAccount's current deposit conditions, so that compatibility match also guarantees every later network fee and receiving-processing outcome without another review."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "This complete fixture permits the next review step, not an unexamined real authorisation."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "3", "feedback": "E: The corrected route's exact identity/network/destination/no-tag/amount conditions match. Continue to the remaining transfer review; no real authorisation or later fee guarantee follows."}, {"id": "PM04B-8", "outcomes": ["O-04.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Pause Unresolved Draft and verify the exact missing network/representation support."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Infer missing fields from the asset's familiar name and continue."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Declare every HBR route permanently impossible."}], "reasons": [{"id": "1", "label": "1", "text": "The unresolved gap needs a specific current receiving-route check, rather than an invented answer."}, {"id": "2", "label": "2", "text": "Familiarity replaces network-specific acceptance information."}, {"id": "3", "label": "3", "text": "One unresolved HBR offer proves every current or future route impossible."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "1", "feedback": "E: Verify the actual missing network/representation support before deciding compatibility. The incomplete offer proves neither success nor permanent impossibility for all routes."}], "outcomes": ["O-04.1", "O-04.2", "O-04.3", "O-04.4"], "prerequisites": ["O-04.1", "O-04.2", "O-04.3"], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-05-A", "canonical_id": "KC-05", "kind": "check", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-05", "title": "Stablecoin and conversion decisions", "fixture_html": "<p>Mapped outcomes: O-05.1–O-05.4. Required: K5A1–K5A8 and both choices per item.</p>\n<p>Fixture: All assets target one USD per token. ReserveDemo reports issuer-held reserves and conditional issuer redemption. CollateralDemo uses crypto collateral and liquidation rules. AlgoDemo attempts supply/incentive adjustment without a stated reserve claim. ReserveDemo's fictional issuer allows direct redemption only for approved institutional accounts meeting stated checks; our learner is not eligible. Market quote today is USD 0.97 per ReserveDemo token. A token holder is not automatically an approved issuer customer. AccountDesk holds customer balances, accepts a submitted conversion order and requires a separately specified bank-payout process. ChainSwap trades through supplied on-chain contracts; it requires an asset-specific spending permission and network fee, and offers tokens rather than a bank transfer.</p>\n<p>For the final comparison use 100 ReserveDemo. Desk A buys them at 150 DEMO-LOCAL per token, deducts a 300 DEMO-LOCAL conversion fee and a 200 DEMO-LOCAL payout fee; payout conditions and a support/dispute channel are explicitly supplied. Seller B offers 155 per token, a 500 conversion fee and an unspecified payout charge; the only claimed payout evidence is B's screenshot. These are fictional offers, not live rates.</p>", "items": [{"id": "K5A1", "outcomes": ["O-05.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Target USD 1; observed quote USD 0.97."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Target USD 0.97; observed quote USD 1."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Target USD 1; observed quote USD 1."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The reserve target determines the exchange quote."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The latest quote changes the reference target."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Reference target and observed price are separate facts."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "C", "feedback": "USD 1 is the reference target; USD 0.97 is the supplied market price. Neither implies the future price."}, {"id": "K5A2", "outcomes": ["O-05.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Classify each as reserve-backed, with different reserve managers."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Classify reserve backing, crypto collateral and supply/incentive adjustment separately."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Classify each as crypto-collateralised, with different liquidation rules."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The descriptions imply different reserve, collateral and incentive risks."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The common reference target establishes a common reserve mechanism."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The common reference target establishes a common collateral mechanism."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Identify all three mechanism families without claiming the classification audits reserves or proves stability."}, {"id": "K5A3", "outcomes": ["O-05.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat possession as sufficient for the next issuer-redemption request."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat AccountDesk conversion as an issuer-redemption request."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat direct issuer redemption as unavailable under these eligibility rules."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "This learner lacks the required issuer-account eligibility."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The token balance satisfies the issuer-account conditions."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The desk quote satisfies the issuer-account conditions."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Actual supplied eligibility, rather than possession, governs direct issuer redemption."}, {"id": "K5A4", "outcomes": ["O-05.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Separate holding, redemption, conversion and payout; inspect restrictions/liquidity."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat conversion approval as completion of redemption and payout."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat reserve reporting as confirmation of redemption and payout access."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The desk and issuer perform the same redemption/payout stages."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The stages have separate terms, authority and failure conditions."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The reserve description establishes the local receiving-account balance."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "B", "feedback": "Distinguish all four stages plus restriction/liquidity conditions; a reserve claim does not prove local payout access."}, {"id": "K5A5", "outcomes": ["O-05.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat both as account-balance orders controlled by service providers."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Distinguish AccountDesk's internal order from ChainSwap's permission-based execution."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat both as contract interactions controlled by the token holder."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Both displayed quotes imply the same custody arrangement."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Both token outputs imply the same execution arrangement."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The supplied controller and execution facts distinguish the routes."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "C", "feedback": "Separate the internal account order from the on-chain contract/permission process. Custody/interface labels alone are not enough."}, {"id": "K5A6", "outcomes": ["O-05.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat the swap's token output as completed local payout."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat the displayed quote as sufficient permission review."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Review spender/scope and execution; verify local payout separately."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The quote establishes neither appropriate authority nor local receipt."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The quote establishes an account credit through the swap."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The quoted output incorporates the separate bank-payout process."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Review consequential authority and the separate payout route. Do not equate swap output with bank settlement."}, {"id": "K5A7", "outcomes": ["O-05.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "A net 15,000; B net remains unknown."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "A net 14,500; B net remains unknown."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "A net 14,500; B net 15,000 confirmed."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "A deducts both fees; B's payout fee remains unspecified."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "A's provider fee is the only charge deducted."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "B's omitted payout charge can be treated as zero."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "A net is 14,500 DEMO-LOCAL. B gross 15,500 less 500 leaves 15,000 before an unknown payout charge, so no complete net comparison."}, {"id": "K5A8", "outcomes": ["O-05.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Prefer A for next review; B needs fees/receiving evidence."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Prefer B for next review on its screenshot/rate alone."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Prefer B for next review, treating its omitted fee as zero."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The higher rate establishes independently received local money."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The screenshot establishes the missing payout charge and receipt."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "A supplies terms; B lacks full cost/receipt evidence."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "C", "feedback": "A can proceed to the next mock review on given terms, with its actual payout evidence still required at receipt. B needs the missing fee and independent receiving record."}], "outcomes": ["O-05.1", "O-05.2", "O-05.3", "O-05.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "KC-05-B", "canonical_id": "KC-05", "kind": "check", "form": "B", "module_id": "M-05", "title": "Retry with eligible redemption and a complete alternative", "fixture_html": "<p>Mapped outcomes: O-05.1–O-05.4. Required: K5B1–K5B8. Do not substitute these facts into form A.</p>\n<p>Fixture: ReserveTwo targets USD 1; market quote is USD 1.02. Its issuer-backed reserve model is distinct from CryptoTwo's volatile crypto collateral/liquidation model and RuleTwo's supply/incentive model. Our fictional organisation has an independently confirmed approved issuer account, meets the supplied redemption minimum/verification conditions, and is not restricted for this example. Direct redemption can be requested at the stated contractual rate, subject to the supplied processing rules; there is no automatic local-currency bank payout. An issuer restriction can affect transfers under the supplied terms, while a thin conversion market can affect executable quotes.</p>\n<p>For 80 tokens, Account R buys at 200 DEMO-LOCAL/token, deducts 500 conversion and 300 payout; its payout record is not yet available. Counterparty S buys at 202, deducts 160 conversion and 200 payout. The supplied exercise independently verifies S's identity, current terms, receiving account and the stated dispute route, and later shows a matching local receiving credit of 15,800. ChainTwo is an on-chain swap route delivering another token, with a declared permission and estimated network fee; Account R controls an internal account conversion.</p>", "items": [{"id": "K5B1", "outcomes": ["O-05.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat USD 1.02 as the revised target and quote."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Separate the USD 1 target from the USD 1.02 quote."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat USD 1 as the target and present quote."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Observed quotes may exceed the stated reference target."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The observed premium revises the issuer's reference target."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The reported reserves establish today's third-party quote."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "A premium is possible in this fixture; target and market quote remain different facts."}, {"id": "K5B2", "outcomes": ["O-05.1"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Classify CryptoTwo as reserve-backed; RuleTwo as crypto-collateralised."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Classify all three as reserve-backed with different issuers."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Classify reserves, crypto collateral and supply/incentive rules separately."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The asset names establish equivalent redemption arrangements."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The stated mechanisms expose different potential failure conditions."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The shared target establishes identical collateral arrangements."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "B", "feedback": "Distinguish all three mechanisms and their risk types, without declaring actual reserve adequacy."}, {"id": "K5B3", "outcomes": ["O-05.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Allow next eligible redemption review; retain separate payout conditions."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Decline next redemption review because token holders cannot qualify."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Allow redemption to the organisation without checking processing conditions."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The token balance itself supplies the required account approval."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The verified account status establishes completed issuer processing."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The organisation qualifies here; redemption and payout remain separate."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "C", "feedback": "Recognise affirmative supplied eligibility. Request permission is not completed redemption or guaranteed local payout."}, {"id": "K5B4", "outcomes": ["O-05.2"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use target price alone to assess transfer/withdrawal access."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Inspect issuer restrictions and market liquidity alongside target price."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Use the premium alone to assess executable conversion/payout."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The stated restrictions/liquidity affect this conversion route."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The premium removes the supplied transfer restriction."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Eligible redemption establishes executable liquidity at Account R."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Issuer restrictions and market liquidity are separate relevant route conditions."}, {"id": "K5B5", "outcomes": ["O-05.3"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Distinguish R's account conversion from ChainTwo's permission-based swap."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Treat R and ChainTwo as separately completed bank payouts."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat R and ChainTwo as issuer-redemption arrangements."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The reference target establishes both routes' controller."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "The supplied controller/execution paths distinguish these routes."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The displayed token output establishes the bank receiving stage."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "B", "feedback": "The controller/execution facts distinguish internal account conversion from the on-chain exchange."}, {"id": "K5B6", "outcomes": ["O-05.3"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat the swap output as net local-currency payout."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Approve the spender on the fee estimate alone."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Review swap authority/output/fees; verify local settlement separately."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "The chain quote contains the separate bank-payout stage."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Quotes establish neither local receipt nor appropriate authority."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The fee estimate establishes a non-spending signature payload."}], "answer_action": "C", "answer_reason": "B", "feedback": "Correctly bounded permission/output/fee checks and separate bank route remain necessary."}, {"id": "K5B7", "outcomes": ["O-05.4"], "class": "C", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "R net 15,200; S net 15,800 DEMO-LOCAL."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "R net 16,000; S net 16,160 DEMO-LOCAL."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "R net 15,500; S net 16,000 DEMO-LOCAL."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Net proceeds deduct both supplied charges from gross."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Compare gross proceeds before subtracting either charge."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Subtract conversion charges while excluding the payout charges."}], "answer_action": "A", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Net arithmetic includes both fees and preserves DEMO-LOCAL units."}, {"id": "K5B8", "outcomes": ["O-05.4"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat S's matched receipt as still unverified despite independent access."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Recognise S's matched independent local credit under supplied terms."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat R's quoted conversion as its completed local payout."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "R's quoted conversion establishes its receiving-account record."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "A conversion quote and receiving credit represent the same stage."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "S's matched independent receipt establishes this specific payout."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "C", "feedback": "Do not teach permanent scepticism of genuine independent receipt. Recognise this matching credit, within its exact case."}], "outcomes": ["O-05.1", "O-05.2", "O-05.3", "O-05.4"], "prerequisites": [], "revision": "1", "approved": false}, {"id": "PM-05-A", "canonical_id": "PM-05", "kind": "mission", "form": "A", "module_id": "M-05", "title": "Compare the whole conversion route", "fixture_html": "<p>Mapped outcomes: O-05.1–O-05.4. Required: K5A1–K5A8 and both choices per item.</p>\n<p>Fixture: All assets target one USD per token. ReserveDemo reports issuer-held reserves and conditional issuer redemption. CollateralDemo uses crypto collateral and liquidation rules. AlgoDemo attempts supply/incentive adjustment without a stated reserve claim. ReserveDemo's fictional issuer allows direct redemption only for approved institutional accounts meeting stated checks; our learner is not eligible. Market quote today is USD 0.97 per ReserveDemo token. A token holder is not automatically an approved issuer customer. AccountDesk holds customer balances, accepts a submitted conversion order and requires a separately specified bank-payout process. ChainSwap trades through supplied on-chain contracts; it requires an asset-specific spending permission and network fee, and offers tokens rather than a bank transfer.</p>\n<p>For the final comparison use 100 ReserveDemo. Desk A buys them at 150 DEMO-LOCAL per token, deducts a 300 DEMO-LOCAL conversion fee and a 200 DEMO-LOCAL payout fee; payout conditions and a support/dispute channel are explicitly supplied. Seller B offers 155 per token, a 500 conversion fee and an unspecified payout charge; the only claimed payout evidence is B's screenshot. These are fictional offers, not live rates.</p><p>Mapped outcomes: O-05.1–O-05.4. Gate: <strong>none; open fictional comparison</strong>. Required: P5A1–P5A6. Use the KC-05-A mechanisms and redemption conditions, but these new offers:</p>\n<p>For 60 ReserveDemo, Acorn Desk quotes 145 DEMO-LOCAL/token, fee 200 conversion plus 100 payout; terms show a minimum 50 tokens, a defined independently accessed dispute channel and a payout still pending. Briar Desk quotes 150, deducts 300 conversion but omits payout fees and local withdrawal restrictions; it supplies only a sender screenshot. Cedar Swap executes a declared on-chain exchange from ReserveDemo to CollateralDemo, proposes a 400-token spending limit despite a 60-token intended swap, and provides no local payout service. Acorn's independently checked account record confirms its stated terms; no actual funds are moved in this exercise.</p>", "items": [{"id": "P5A1", "outcomes": ["O-05.1"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Treat the USD 1 target as the current price across models."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Separate target/quote and the reserve/collateral/incentive model risks."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Treat USD 0.97 as the issuer-redemption rate across models."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Shared target does not erase mechanism or trading-price differences."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Mechanism descriptions establish the same redemption protection."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The local desk rate establishes the token's reference target."}], "answer_action": "B", "answer_reason": "A", "feedback": "Establish target versus quote and all three mechanisms; no guaranteed target-price assumption."}, {"id": "P5A2", "outcomes": ["O-05.2"], "class": "E", "prompt": "Choose the finding or action and its reason.", "actions": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "Use token possession as sufficient for direct issuer redemption."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Use Acorn's internal order as completed issuer redemption."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "Exclude direct redemption here; assess conversion/payout terms separately."}], "reasons": [{"id": "A", "label": "A", "text": "This token quantity substitutes for issuer-account eligibility."}, {"id": "B", "label": "B", "text": "Eligibility and stage conditions govern the available route."}, {"id": "C", "label": "C", "text": "The conversion quote confirms the issuer-account approval."}], "answer_action"